description=Quality-of-life tools for Project Zomboid. Highlights loose items on the ground, including items added by other mods.<LINE><LINE>
description=Controls: Click Items: ON/OFF in the left sidebar. F8 is the default optional shortcut.<LINE>
description=Settings: Change the shortcut, colour, radius and enabled state in Options > Mods > PZ Survivor Toolkit.<LINE><LINE>
description=Visibility: Only items in your character's current field of view are highlighted. Previously explored tiles alone are not enough.<LINE>
description=Rendering: Uses native outlines or colour tints, depending on the item renderer.<LINE><LINE>
description=Clothing comparisons: Optional neutral grey for zero changes in the Wear menu. Gains and losses retain the game's configured colours.<LINE><LINE>
description=Multiplayer auto-drink: Respects each player's own setting, including changes in Options. The host's saved preference no longer blocks other players.<LINE><LINE>
description=CleanUI / Container Capacity Indicator: Aligns bars with visible inventory icons, including hidden equipment and scaled icons. Load order: CleanUI, PZSurvivorToolkit, ContainerCapacityIndicator.<LINE><LINE>
description=TV & Radio ReInvented: Keeps player windows open on outside clicks and adds a close button; configurable in Mod Options. Fixes native macOS video paths using the installed mod directory.<LINE><LINE>
description=Compatibility: Build 42.19 or newer within Build 42. No additional mod dependencies. Auto-drink tested with two local multiplayer clients on B42.21. Split-screen has not been verified.<LINE><LINE>
description=Source: https://github.com/AlexRedby/pz-survivor-toolkit
versionMin=42.19
